Hello LKML,

for some time we experience kernel panics in VMs running=20
on Qemu with RBD devices in the sym53c8xx driver (see attachements).

We see at least the following kernels affected:

    3.2.0-4-amd64 (Debian stable)
    3.16.0-4-amd64 (Debian Jessie)
    3.16.0-0.bpo.4-amd64 (Debian backports)

We experience this problem mostly when having high i/o in the VM
and/or load due to rebalancing data.

I was wondering if this can be fixed in the kernel or if it needs to be
addressed differently by changing qemu/ceph parameters.

Our qemu parameters (coming from opennebula) are

    qemu-system-x86_64 -enable-kvm -name one-204 -S -machine pc-i440fx-trus=
ty,accel=3Dkvm,usb=3Doff -m 512 -realtime mlock=3Doff -smp 2,sockets=3D2,co=
res=3D1,threads=3D1 -uuid d7c3374e-349e-4db6-8f54-f3c607f93101 -no-user-con=
fig -nodefaults -chardev socket,id=3Dcharmonitor,path=3D/var/lib/libvirt/qe=
mu/one-204.monitor,server,nowait -mon chardev=3Dcharmonitor,id=3Dmonitor,mo=
de=3Dcontrol -rtc base=3Dutc -no-shutdown -boot strict=3Don -device piix3-u=
sb-uhci,id=3Dusb,bus=3Dpci.0,addr=3D0x1.0x2 -device lsi,id=3Dscsi0,bus=3Dpc=
i.0,addr=3D0x4 -drive file=3Drbd:one/one-53-204-0:id=3Dlibvirt:key=3D...:au=
th_supported=3Dcephx\;none:mon_host=3Dkaffee.private.ungleich.ch\;wein.priv=
ate.ungleich.ch\;tee.private.ungleich.ch,if=3Dnone,id=3Ddrive-scsi0-0-0,for=
mat=3Draw,cache=3Dnone -device scsi-hd,bus=3Dscsi0.0,scsi-id=3D0,drive=3Ddr=
ive-scsi0-0-0,id=3Dscsi0-0-0,bootindex=3D1 -drive file=3D/var/lib/one//data=
stores/0/204/disk.1,if=3Dnone,id=3Ddrive-ide0-0-0,readonly=3Don,format=3Dra=
w -device ide-cd,bus=3Dide.0,unit=3D0,drive=3Ddrive-ide0-0-0,id=3Dide0-0-0 =
-netdev tap,fd=3D24,id=3Dhostnet0 -device rtl8139,netdev=3Dhostnet0,id=3Dne=
t0,mac=3D02:00:4d:6d:96:ae,bus=3Dpci.0,addr=3D0x3 -vnc 0.0.0.0:204 -device =
cirrus-vga,id=3Dvideo0,bus=3Dpci.0,addr=3D0x2 -device virtio-balloon-pci,id=
=3Dballoon0,bus=3Dpci.0,addr=3D0x5

where

    -device lsi,id=3Dscsi0,bus=3Dpci.0,addr=3D0x4

is probably the relevant parameter.

Cheers,

Nico

